  "notes": "FORMS:\n{黙|もく} (silence) + {秘|ひ} (secret) → keeping silent\n{黙秘|もくひ}する (to remain silent, to refuse to answer)\n\nLEGAL TERM:\n{黙秘|もくひ}{権|けん} (right to remain silent) - A constitutional right in Japan protecting individuals from self-incrimination.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {黙秘|もくひ}を{貫|つらぬ}く (to maintain silence)\n- {黙秘|もくひ}を{破|やぶ}る (to break silence)\n- {完全|かんぜん}{黙秘|もくひ} (complete silence)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {供述|きょうじゅつ} (statement, testimony)\n- {自白|じはく} (confession)",
